  "summary": "Malicious code in beaver-ui-side-navigation (npm)",
  "details": "Beaver-ui-side-navigation@35.7.1 is a trojanized \"React components\" package whose index.js loads a hidden dropper (_helpers.js). On import the dropper fingerprints the OS/architecture, downloads a second-stage binary over HTTPS from Cloudflare Workers endpoints (oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, /pkg/package.exe), and falls back to a DNS-TXT command channel via c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru. The downloaded payload is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e (or dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe in %TEMP% on Windows), made executable, and launched as a detached background process (cmd.exe /c start /b on Windows, /bin/sh -c on POSIX).",
  "affected": [
